{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"support of a module support of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md","fileName":"Support of a Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Support of a Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:05\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Associated Primes and Module Dimension]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Associated Primes and Module Dimension","Associated Prime","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"support of a module support of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md","fileName":"Support of a Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Support of a Module","heading":"Support of a Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The support Supp(M) of an R-module is the set of prime ideals p for which the localization M_p is nonzero. It identifies where the module remains visible on the ring's spectrum.\n\nFor a finitely generated module, support consists exactly of primes containing Ann(M). Every [[Associated Prime]] belongs to the support, and every support prime contains an associated prime.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Associated Primes and Module Dimension","Associated Prime","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"support of a module support of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Support of a Module.md","fileName":